  clock: 3  # a55b
  nonce: a55b  # a55b
  message: "Fixed in PR #1744 (dev dbeef1ab2a). ddg_build.return_statement_spans now gives an expression body (JS/TS arrow without a block, python lambda) one return span over the body, and a Rust block's tail expression a return span (cfg_nodes/rust.yaml block_tail_returns: true; statements/items ending the block do not count). BEHAVIORAL REPRO, re-run on merged dev with verify-claims host_secret -> subprocess: rs_tail (fn get() -> String { env::var(\"TOOL\").unwrap() }) violated, was confirmed_with_caveats; js_arrow (const get = () => process.env.TOOL) violated, was confirmed_with_caveats; the explicit-return controls rs_return/js_return stay violated. A/B on real repos: aardvark-dns and apollo-server moved nothing; ripgrep host-secret-no-host-fs 3 -> 8 rows and host-secret-no-logging 1 -> 2 (new rows are lifted sources from tail-expression helpers, e.g. config.rs args() RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH), and no verdict changed. NOT DONE: the Python lambda still reads confirmed_with_caveats because the analyzer emits a name-bound lambda as a variable and the python DDG spec has no lambda; filed as WI-rosun."  # a55b
